/E (In view of representations received highlighting delays in issuance of TDS certificates for the quarter ending 31st December 2025 due to technical glitches on the e-filing portal, the Board has acknowledged the genuine hardship faced by deductors in meeting the prescribed timelines. Accordingly, in exercise of its powers under Section 119 of the Income-tax Act, 1961, the due date for issuance of TDS certificates for the said quarter has been extended to 31st March 2026. This relaxation provides relief to deductors impacted by system-related issues and ensures that procedural non-compliance arising from circumstances beyond their control does not attract penal consequences.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
